there is a new report from axios  reporter jonathan swann  which tells the story of a donald trump  temper tantrum in which after losing the  2020 election trump tried to just pull  troops from around the world now you  might think that's great i want to bring  our troops home we shouldn't have troops  all over the world the way that we do  and i would agree with you but this was  not a foreign policy calculation by  donald trump this was not a well-crafted  decision to reduce the military presence  around the world this was not uh  a calculated  and uh much discussed  uh strategy for reducing the spread of  the american military throughout the  globe this was a temper tantrum over  losing the election on november 9th of  2020 you might remember that's the day  after the media finally said okay joe  biden won  john mcentee one of donald trump's  favorite aides  gave a note  to army colonel colonel douglas mcgregor  and on that note it said this is what  the president wants you to do  get us out of afghanistan get us out of  iraq and syria  withdraw completely from germany and get  us completely out of africa and mcgregor  explained you know we can't really just  do this by january 20th  and i certainly just can't do it by  myself and mcentee said to mcgregor well  do what you can  and mcgregor said i really can't do  anything i need like a real order from  the president i can't just go and pull  all of our troops from around the world  two days later and this is all based on  jonathan swan's axios reporting such a  letter was delivered to the acting  secretary of defense christopher miller  all u.s military forces are to be  withdrawn from somalia by december 31st  all u.s forces are to be withdrawn from  afghanistan by january 15th with similar  unrealistic dates and miller wondered  what the hell is going on here the  department of defense called the white  house lawyer pat chipoloni and asked  what is going on here they called  trump's national security adviser robert  o'brien  no one had any idea what was going on  this wasn't a plan  this wasn't policy this was just a very  strange temper tantrum and as jonathan  swann writes for axios the u.s  government's top national security  leaders soon realized they were dealing  with an off the books operation by trump  himself  ultimately it didn't happen but as you  can see this is not the action of a  president who wanted to do these things  because they were the right things to do  if they were he wouldn't have waited  until november 9th of the last year of  his first term to do it it was a  triggered tilted man  furious that he lost  seemingly wanting to create as much  chaos as possible for joe biden who  would be replacing him just two months  later and as jonathan swann writes quote  christopher miller told associates he  had three goals for the finer final  weeks of the trump administration number  one no major war  number two no military coup and number  three no troops fighting citizens on the  streets of the united states  think about the insanity of the  situation  when the acting national security  adviser acting secretary of defense  says my goals for the lame duck period  are preventing trump from starting a war  preventing trump from using the military  for a coup and preventing trump from  deploying troops to fight citizens on  the streets of the united states the  more we read stories like this one the  more we realize just how insanely close  we came  to an even greater level of chaos the  stuff that was apparently narrowly  avoided  almost makes the january sixth  insurrection look relatively mild in  comparison and between the riots  and trump trying to overturn the  election results and stay in power and  on a whim saying pull all troops from  everywhere and having lawyers in and  talking about martial law  or seizing voting machines or whatever  else  the stuff that happened is bad enough  but look at all of the things we're  learning about that almost happened and  as i've said when donald trump left  it was way worse than we knew  over time we're going to learn more  but i don't know that we'll ever really  learn the full scope of exactly how bad  it was and this is just yet another  thing and it i know that you know there  are probably going to be people in my  audience i've already seen it in other  enclaves there's probably some people in  my audience who maybe identify with what  is sometimes called the revolutionary  left who will say this was trump  outflanking the left on the spread of  the  american military trump was trying to  pull troops from all these places that  troops arguably shouldn't even be in and  now leftists like david pakman uh are  saying that it was a bad idea i'm not  saying it was a bad idea and i've been  arguing for drawing down troops in  germany and in many other places for a  decade on this program the point is this  wasn't policy this was the day after the  election was called for biden trump  without consulting with anyone and for  no strategic reason for no well thought  out foreign policy reason just says i'm  going to create an s storm for lack of a  better term for joe biden and just start  pulling troops haphazardly it is not  policy and this is not how anybody who  is a thinking individual would say it  should be done we should be drawing down  troops we should be reducing our  military footprint there's no question  about it but if you do it as policy you  don't do it once you're already a lame  duck that doesn't make any sense and  that's pathetic  i'm really excited that one of our  sponsors today is helix sleep i sleep on  a helix mattress at home i absolutely  love it and that's why i reached out to  them about sponsoring the david pakman  show  buying a mattress in the past  was always a huge guessing game for me i  didn't know what i actually needed i  didn't know what i would like but helix  has a sleep quiz on their website you  tell them your body type your sleeping 